replace audioserver->hal_audio_sonos binder: add `call`. APS calls getAudioPorts() on the HAL; without call it is denied and APS drops the module (permissive avc 2026-11-25: denied {call} comm=audioserver tcontext=hal_audio_sonos).
default_android_service add: the daemon registers IModule/sonos + sonos_audio_module with the SYSTEM servicemanager, which labels both default_android_service (vendor service_contexts are not read by it). Broad: lets this domain register any name falling to the default label. Accepted on this single-purpose panel; the narrow fix needs a system service_contexts rebuild.
vendor_configs_file read: daemon reads /vendor/etc/sonos_zones.conf.
servicemanager binder/dir/file/process: registration path with the system servicemanager (binder_use equivalent for this domain).
udp_socket getopt/setopt: discovery sets IP_MULTICAST_TTL on its SSDP M-SEARCH socket (unbound; no :1900 bind, no multicast join).
netdomain membership: discovery opens TCP to :1400 and UDP SSDP; Android requires every socket-creating domain to reach netd fwmarkd (on-device 2026-11-25: denied { write } name="fwmarkd" scontext=hal_audio_sonos). netdomain is the standard attribute that grants it, as used by the wifi/rild HALs in this same policy.
append/etc/selinux/vendor_service_contexts: IModule/sonos fell back to default_android_service, which audioserver may not find (avc find, build 20261126T003439Z). Label it hal_audio_service like every other IModule.
(allow hal_audio_sonos hal_audio_service (service_manager (add find))): lets the HAL register under that label.
property set rules + append/etc/init/sonos_audio_service.rc: audioserver reads module ports once at boot, before the network is up (build 20261126T005544Z served 0 rooms while discovery later found 11). The HAL sets vendor.sonos.rooms_gen when it finds rooms audioserver has not read (no cap; 5 s settle, 30 s apart; rooms that power off stay listed, so only a never-seen room triggers); the rc restarts audioserver so it re-reads.
vendor_property_contexts vendor.sonos.name. + vendor_public_default_prop set: the HAL publishes each player's room name by IP; system_server (which may read vendor_public_default_prop) names each output route from it, since audio policy drops device port names.
remove app/ShowerCast: the Sonos rooms are native output devices; no app belongs in the audio path.
Sonos rooms are a module in the reference audio service (hal_audio_default): it gets the network (SSDP discovery, UPnP control, HTTP stream) and property-set rights the standalone daemon had; the daemon and its rc are removed.
